Transfer by aircraft, vessel, or other means of transportation as referred to in Subpar-agraph 1 of Paragraph 1 of Article 19 of the Act shall be limited to the following cir-cumstances:
1. Flight crew members or cabin crew members arriving aboard an aircraft or other similar means of air transportation and subsequently transferring to another air-craft or similar means of air transportation;
2. Vessel crew members or service personnel arriving aboard a vessel or other similar means of maritime transportation and subsequently transferring to another air-craft or similar means of air transportation;
3. Vessel crew members or service personnel arriving aboard a vessel or other similar means of maritime transportation and subsequently transferring to another vessel or similar means of maritime transportation.
4. Any other special cases involving transfers between aircraft, vessels, or other means of transportation, as deemed necessary by the National Immigration Agency, Minis-try of the Interior (hereinafter referred to as the NIA).

Other legitimate reasons referred to in Subparagraph 4 of Paragraph 1 of Article 19 of the Act are limited to the following circumstances:
1. Flight crew members or cabin crew members temporarily entering the State in the performance of their flight duties;
2. Vessel crew members or service personnel aboard a maritime vessel temporarily entering the State in the performance of their voyage duties ;
3. Any other special cases approved by the NIA.

Foreign nationals applying for a Temporary Entry Permit shall complete an application and submit their applications to the NIA in accordance with the following rules:
1. Applicants falling under Subparagraph 1 of Article 3 of the Regulations shall have the transportation operator attach a valid foreign passport, flight crew certificate and proof of flight assignment before boarding;
2. Applicants falling under Subparagraph 2 or 3 of Article 3 of the Regulations shall have the transport operator attach a valid foreign passport, seafarer’s book and proof of vessel assignment before the applicants temporarily enter the State;
3. Applicants falling under Subparagraph 4 of Article 3 of the Regulations shall have the captain of the aircraft or vessel or transport operator attach a valid foreign passport, flight crew certificate, seafarer’s book or a photocopy of other identifica-tion documents, together with a confirmed ticket for a connecting flight or vessel scheduled for the same day or the nearest available departure before boarding an aircraft or vessel;
4. Applicants falling under Subparagraph 1 or 2 of the preceding Article shall have the captain of the aircraft or vessel or transport operator attach a valid foreign passport, flight crew certificate, or seafarer’s book, and proof of assignment before temporarily entering the State;
5. Applicants that are subject to Subparagraph 3 of the preceding Article shall have the captain of the aircraft or vessel or transport operator attach a valid foreign passport, crew certificate, seafarer’s book, a photocopy of other identification doc-uments, or proof of assignment before boarding an aircraft or vessel.
In accordance with Subparagraph 2 or 3 of Paragraph 1 of Article 19 of the Act, foreign nationals who have not applied for a Temporary Entry Permit before entry, the flight or vessel captain, transport operator, the authority conducting the rescue mission, or flight or vessel captain who undertakes the rescue mission shall submit a name list in lieu of the temporary entry application to the NIA after the foreign national’s tempo-rary entry. Where, due to unavoidable accidents or disasters, no application for a Temporary Entry Permit is filed, the NIA shall notify the relevant embassy, consulate, or authorized representative office of the foreign national. If no application is filed, and the foreign national’s country or region of nationality has no embassy, consulate, or authorized representative office in the State, or if the foreign national is stateless or of undetermined nationality, the NIA shall, upon verification, grant the foreign na-tional temporary entry into the State or take other necessary measures.

Applicants for temporary entry by foreign nationals may be denied under any of the following circumstances. Applicants who meet the condition of Subparagraph 2 or 3 of Paragraph 1 of Article 19 of the Act are not subject to this limitation.
1. Unable to provide all of the documents listed in Article 5;
2. Circumstances specified in Subparagraphs 1 to 8 and Subparagraphs 11 to 16 of Paragraph 1 of Article 18 of the Act;
3. Circumstances specified in Paragraph 2 of Article 18 of the Act;
4. Having violated Subparagraph 4 or 5 of Paragraph 1 of Article 7 of the Regulations;
5. As specified by other laws and regulations.

Foreign nationals who have applied for and have been authorized to enter the State temporarily will be issued a Temporary Entry Permit. The Permit shall include the fol-lowing information:
1. Name, nationality, date of birth, gender, personal identification number, and tem-porary address of stay; if an applicant also holds R.O.C. (Taiwan) nationality, the permit shall also indicate his/her Chinese name;
2. The purpose, relevant facts, reasons, and legal basis therefor;
3. The length of stay;
4. The place of stay;
5. Additional conditions.
For applicants who have been authorized in accordance with Subparagraph 2 or 3 of Paragraph 1 of Article 19 of the Act, the Temporary Entry Permit may exclude the infor-mation listed in the preceding Subparagraph 1. The Temporary Entry Permit may also be substituted with a name list bearing the official stamp of the NIA.
Foreign nationals who apply for temporary entry but are not granted approval shall be issued a notification of denial. The notification shall also indicate the information speci-fied in Subparagraphs 1 and 2 of Paragraph 1 of this Article.
